      },
      "content": "What is the idiomatic way to read a text file line by line without loading all of it into memory?",
      "created_at": "2026-10-12T08:31:00Z",
      "edited_at": null,
      "is_solution": false
    },
    {
      "id": "01a12f5b-ae60-70b7-a33e-97e3451cda97",
      "number": 2,
      "parent_id": null,
      "author": {
        "id": "019792ae-83c0-793e-a9d2-510cbd597653",
        "username": "ana.lima",
        "display_name": "Ana Lima"
      },
      "content": "Wrap the file in a `BufReader` and use `lines()`:\n\n```rust\nuse std::fs::File;\nuse std::io::{self, BufRead, BufReader};\n\nfn main() -> io::Result<()> {\n    for line in BufReader::new(File::open(\"log.txt\")?).lines() {\n        println!(\"{}\", line?);\n    }\n    Ok(())\n}\n```",
      "created_at": "2026-10-12T09:05:00Z",
      "edited_at": null,
      "is_solution": true
    },
    {
      "id": "01a13e91-6b40-7104-b0c0-0e253bd4ec91",
      "number": 3,
      "parent_id": "01a12f5b-ae60-70b7-a33e-97e3451cda97",
      "author": {
        "id": "0194f481-44a0-7f90-ab3d-189d8506bb3a",
        "username": "ferris",
        "display_name": "Ferris"
      },
      "content": "Note that `lines()` strips the `\\n` (and a `\\r\\n`). Use `read_line` if you need the line endings.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-15T07:58:00Z",
      "edited_at": null,
      "is_solution": false
    }
  ],
